# Stable, vendor-neutral URLs for everything published on a release.
#
# One splat covers the verification files, the installers, and the updater manifests, so
# nothing we document or ship has to name the GitHub organisation. That matters twice over.
# The org was renamed from Sparcle-LLC to SparcleHQ and the company is Sparcle Inc, so a raw
# release URL prints a legal name we no longer use in front of the person verifying a
# download. And it moves the indirection onto a domain we own, so the backing store can change
# later without breaking anything that already points here.
#
# The updater endpoint compiled into shipped clients still names Sparcle-LLC directly and works
# only through GitHub's org-rename redirect, which is a dependency we do not control. Future
# builds should point at this path instead. That helps new builds only, since the endpoint is
# baked in at build time, which is the reason to start soon rather than later.
/releases/latest/*  https://github.com/SparcleHQ/sparcle.app/releases/latest/download/:splat  302
